2. Fight for a Refund From Spain
By paying as a "Deposit," you keep your legal escalation (appeal) alive.
Once you are safely in Spain with your job and residency, the National Road Safety Authority (ANSR) will eventually read your appeal [ch. 1297].
When you present the proof that you did have an active insurance policy (even if the plates were irregular), they will often reduce the massive "no insurance" fine down to a minor administrative registration error and refund the difference back to your bank account.
